    <desc>Choose whether new terminals open in tabs or windows, and where new tabs go.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Windows and tabs</title>

<p>You can choose whether <gui style="menuitem">New Terminal</gui> in the
  context menu, and <app>Pano Terminal</app> started from the command line
  without the <cmd>--tab</cmd> or <cmd>--window</cmd> option, open a new tab
  or a new window:</p>
  <steps>
<item><p>Press the menu button in the top-right corner of the window and select <gui style="menuitem">Preferences</gui>.</p></item>
<item><p>In the <gui>Behavior</gui> group, set <gui>Open New Terminals</gui> to <gui>In Tab</gui> or <gui>In Window</gui>.</p></item>
</steps>

  <p><gui>New Tab Position</gui> in the same group sets whether new tabs go
  after the last tab or next to the current one.</p>

